      "comment": "Returns a constant true value for success indication or initialization callback\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load immediate value 1 into EAX return register\n2. Execute return instruction with stack cleanup\n3. Transfer control back to calling function\n\nParameters:\n(none) - Function takes no input parameters\n\nReturns:\nint - Always returns 1 indicating success, true condition, or positive result\n     Used as a simple boolean true provider in initialization sequences\n\nSpecial Cases:\nThis function serves as a constant success indicator, commonly used as:\n- Default callback in function pointer tables\n- Initialization success stub\n- Boolean true provider for conditional logic\nThe __stdcall convention with RET 0xc suggests compatibility with specific\ncalling interfaces that expect parameter cleanup.",
